|passage=NOW, THEREFORE, I, Gerald R. Ford, President of the United States, pursuant to the '''pardon''' power conferred upon me by Article II, Section 2, of the Constitution, have granted and by these presents do grant a full, free, and absolute '''pardon''' unto Richard Nixon for all offenses against the United States which he, Richard Nixon, has committed or may have committed or taken part in during the period from July{{sic|January}} 20, 1969 through August 9, 1974.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=2001
|author=w:Barbara Olson
|chapter=The Final Frenzy: Finishing Touches on the Legend
|title=The Final Days: The Last, Desperate Abuses of Power by the Clinton White House
