#: {{ux|en|I sat by my sister's bed, '''peeling''' oranges for her.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Merchant of Venice|act=I|scene=iii|passage=The skillful shepherd '''peeled''' me certain wands.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To remove something from the outer or top layer of.
#: {{ux|en|I '''peeled''' (the skin from) a banana and ate it hungrily.}}
#: {{ux|en|We '''peeled''' the old wallpaper off in strips where it was hanging loose.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To become detached, come away, especially in flakes or strips; to shed skin in such a way.
#: {{ux|en|I had been out in the sun too long, and my nose was starting to '''peel'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To remove one's clothing.
#: {{ux|en|The children '''peeled''' by the side of the lake and jumped in.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[move]], [[separate]] (off or away).
#: {{ux|en|The scrum-half '''peeled''' off and made for the touchlines.}}

