====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# The [[skin#Noun|skin]] of an [[animal]] with the [[hair#Noun|hair]] or [[wool#Noun|wool]] on; either a [[raw#Adjective|raw]] or [[undressed#Adjective|undressed]] [[hide#Noun|hide]], or a skin [[preserve#Verb|preserved]] with the hair or wool on it (sometimes [[wear#Verb|worn]] as a [[garment#Noun|garment]] with [[minimal#Adjective|minimal]] [[modification]]).
#* {{RQ:Jefferies Amateur Poacher|chapter=The First Gun|page=1|passage=Perhaps the reason why he [a stuffed fox] seemed in such a ghastly rage was that he did not come by his death fairly. Otherwise his '''pelt''' would not have been so perfect. And why else was he put away up there out of sight?—and so magnificent a brush as he had too.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=[[w:E. C. Vivian|E[velyn] Charles Vivian]]|title=White Man’s Magic: A Story of the Canadian Mounted Police|newspaper=[[w:The Boy's Own Paper|The Boy’s Own Paper]]|location=London|publisher=“Boy’s Own Paper” Office,{{nb...|4 Bouverie Street, E.C.}}|month=July|year=1922|volume=XLV, part 9|page=617|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=IsPnAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA617|column=1|oclc=870086995|passage=My people got themselves '''pelts''' and '''pelts'''—there was such a trapping as comes but few times in a life. '''Pelts''' and '''pelts''', the silver and the grey—fine '''pelts'''.}}
# {{lb|en|also|figuratively}} The skin of an animal (especially a [[goat#Noun|goat]] or [[sheep]]) with the hair or wool [[remove#Verb|removed]], often in [[preparation]] for [[tanning#Noun|tanning]].
# The [[fur#Noun|fur]] or hair of a [[living#Adjective|living]] animal.
#: {{nearsyn|en|coat#Noun}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Georgics|book=3|lines=670–673|page=116|passage=The Cauſes and the Signs ſhall next be told, / Of ev'ry Sickneſs that infects the Fold [of sheep]. / A ſcabby Tetter on their '''pelts''' vvill ſtick, / VVhen the ravv Rain has pierc'd 'em to the quick: {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|Ireland|humorous|informal}} [[human#Adjective|Human]] skin, especially when [[bare#Adjective|bare]]; also, a [[person#Noun|person]]'s hair.
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Age of Consent|page=177|passage=Put on your dress, ye shameless witch, standin' there in your '''pelt''' I'll take a strap to, for havin' the conceit out of you, for by your idling had lost me the sup of gin to keep the breath of life in me. Cover your scut, or I'll welt the skin off it.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}}
## A garment [[make#Verb|made]] from animal skins.
## {{lb|en|falconry}} The [[body#Noun|body]] of any [[quarry#Noun|quarry]] [[kill#Verb|killed]] by a [[hawk#Noun|hawk]]; also, a [[dead#Adjective|dead]] [[bird#Noun|bird]] [[give#Verb|given]] to a hawk for [[food]].
##* {{RQ:R. F. Burton Falconry|chapter=A Day with the Bashah|page=60|passage=If two [hawks] are flown they are certain to fell the game at once, and the falconer is always flurried by their violent propensity to crab over the "'''pelt'''."}}

