#* {{quote-text|en|year=1903|author=Maxwell Gray|title=Richard Rosny|page=210
|passage="You will take pleasure in '''parishing'''. Mother used to '''parish'''."<br>"How do you know I like '''parishing'''?"<br>"Your uncle said so."<br>"Oh! did he?"<br>"And you may like the rectory people; it's a fine old house, and often full of visitors."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1921|author=Margaret Pedler|title=The Splendid Folly|page=46
|passage="Are you going ‘'''parishing'''’ this morning?" inquired Diana, as she watched him fill and light his pipe.}}
