===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*perh₃-}}
Recorded c.1430, "division into shares, distinction," from {{inh|en|enm|particioun}}, from {{der|en|fro|particion}} (modern {{m|fr|partition}}), from {{der|en|la|partitio|partitio, partitionem|division, portion}}, from {{m|la|partitus}}, the past participle of {{m|la|partio|partire|to split (up), part(ition)}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/pɑːˈtɪ.ʃən/|[pʰɑːˈtʰɪ.ʃn̩]|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-partition.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/pɑɹˈtɪ.ʃən/|[pʰɑɹˈtʰɪ.ʃn̩]|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪʃən|s=3}}
* {{hyph|en|par|ti|tion}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# An action which [[divide]]s a thing into parts, or [[separate]]s one thing from another.
#: {{ux|en|the {{w|Partitions of Poland|'''partitions''' of Poland}}}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 4-2|act=IV|scene=i|passage=And good from bad find no '''partition'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1958 May|title=Decline in Irish Railway Mileage|journal=Railway Magazine|page=295|text=At the '''partition''' of Ireland in 1920, the railway mileage of the whole country stood at its maximum figure of 3,442, of which 2,668 miles were in the South, and 754 in the much smaller North.}}
# A [[part]] of something that has been [[divide]]d.
#: {{ux|en|the {{w|Russian Partition|Russian '''Partition'''}}}}
# {{lb|en|math}} An approach to [[division]] in which one asks what the size of each [[part]] is, rather than (as in [[quotition]]) how many parts there are.
# The [[division]] of a [[territory]] into two or more [[autonomous]] ones.
#: {{ux|en|Monarchies where '''partition''' isn't prohibited risk weakening through parcellation and civil wars between the heirs.}}
# A [[vertical]] structure that divides a [[room]].
#: {{ux|en|a brick '''partition'''; lath and plaster '''partitions'''}}
# That which divides or separates; that by which different things, or distinct parts of the same thing, are separated; boundary; dividing line or space.
#* {{RQ:Dryden Fables|The Flower and the Leaf
|passage=No sight could pass / Betwixt the nice '''partitions''' of the grass.}}
# A part divided off by walls; an apartment; a compartment.
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=8|passage=Lodged in a small '''partition'''.|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} The [[severance]] of common or undivided interests, particularly in [[real estate]]. It may be effected by consent of parties, or by compulsion of law.
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[section]] of a [[hard disk]] separately [[formatted]].
#: {{hypo|en|extended partition|primary partition|swap partition}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=Bungie|authorlink=Bungie|title=w:Halo 3|publisher=w:Microsoft Game Studios|date=25 September 2007|system=w:Xbox 360|level=[https://www.halopedia.org/Terminal_(Halo_3)#The_terminals Terminal Three (Legendary)]|passage=The epicenter of the disturbance is the '''partition''' currently housing a [personality construct array] retrieved from Contender AI 05-032 <+> 0816.}}
# {{lb|en|databases}} A [[division]] of a [[database]] or one of its constituting elements such as [[table]]s into separate independent parts.
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[division]] of a [[data]] [[stream]], such as a [[messaging]] [[queue]] or [[topic]] (often representing a unit of [[parallelism]], and of [[fault tolerance]]). 
# {{lb|en|set theory}} A collection of non-empty, [[disjoint]] [[subset]]s of a [[set]] whose [[union]] is the set itself (i.e. all elements of the set are contained in exactly one of the subsets).
# {{lb|en|music}} A [[musical]] [[score]].

